{"availability":"available","full":"abird-ai/dotlink","name":"dotlink","description":"Simply @ dotlink anywhere in ChatGPT — chat, space, or your dot to work with files on your machine, use local tools and projects you exposed — securely, from a single binary.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-30T03:56:54Z","updated":"2026-10-02T12:45:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Simply @dotlink anywhere in ChatGPT — chat, space, or your dot to work with files on your machine, use local tools and projects you exposed — securely, from a single binary.","A single lightweight binary with an MCP server, OpenAI tunnel transport, permission engine, profiles, activity logging, and a full Bubblewrap sandbox on Linux — no UI, no third-party relay, guided setup.","When your machine is offline, keep planning against context already in ChatGPT; reconnect later and let ChatGPT re-read the live project before continuing."],"features":["Let your ChatGPT Web and your dot work directly on your computer through controlled, fine-grained access: read and edit files, run Git, build, test, execute scripts, and use only the tools you explicitly expose.","Give ChatGPT controlled access to several machines without installing the ChatGPT desktop app or provisioning SSH: run dotlink on each machine and expose only the projects, files, and capabilities you choose.","Use local data without the upload/download loop: analyze files, build reports or slide decks, and work with artifacts directly from your machine.","Use ChatGPT as a practical fallba